The one sentence you'll never forget

File (or Path) tells Java where the file is. Streams (FileReader, FileWriter, FileInputStream, FileOutputStream) and the Files class perform the actual reading and writing.

Learning roadmap (in order)
File – represent a file or directory path.
FileReader / FileWriter – read and write text.
BufferedReader / BufferedWriter – faster text I/O.
FileInputStream / FileOutputStream – binary files.
Path and Files (NIO) – modern, preferred API for many tasks.
Try-with-resources – automatically closes files and is the recommended way to manage streams.

If you master these six topics, you'll understand almost every file-handling scenario you'll encounter in Java interviews and Spring Boot applications.
